Unverified: this recipe runs a full GCC build/install (gmake DESTDIR=...
install) despite the description promising "libstdc++ and libgcc_s
runtime only" - nothing here scopes it down to just those two, and the
libgcc_s.so.1/libstdc++.so.6 files actually present in build sysroots
turned out to be untracked stray files (`scraps owns` found no owner for
libgcc_s.so.1), not something this recipe produced. It has probably never
actually been built successfully.

Also missing regardless of how it gets built: the unversioned dev
symlinks (libgcc_s.so -> libgcc_s.so.1, libstdc++.so -> libstdc++.so.6).
Only the runtime SONAME files exist - anything passing -lgcc_s/-lstdc++
to the linker (rustc's own build did) fails with "unable to find library"
even though the actual .so.N files are sitting right there, because the
linker looks for the plain unversioned name specifically. Add those two
`ln -sf` lines to package() whenever this recipe is actually made to
build for real instead of copying the files in from wherever they came
from before.
